{"name":"Chef’s Hat","hex":"#f3f4f5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chef","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The presiding cook in the kitchen of a large household.","The head cook of a restaurant or other establishment."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To work as a chef; to prepare and cook food professionally.","To stab with a knife, to shank."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chef"},{"term":"hat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Haitian Creole."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A covering for the head, often in the approximate form of a cone, dome or  cylinder closed at its top end, and sometimes having a brim and other decoration.","A particular role or capacity that a person might fill."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chef's uniform","blocks":[{"text":"The traditional chef's uniform includes a toque blanche, white double-breasted jacket, pants in a black-and-white houndstooth pattern, and apron. It is a common occupational uniform in the Western world. The chef's buttons also have a meaning: while qualified chefs wear black buttons, students wear white buttons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/William_Orpen_Le_Chef_de_l%27H%C3%B4tel_Chatham%2C_Paris.jpg/330px-William_Orpen_Le_Chef_de_l%27H%C3%B4tel_Chatham%2C_Paris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chef's_uniform"},{"title":"Hat","blocks":[{"text":"A hat is a head covering which is worn for various reasons, including protection against weather conditions, ceremonial reasons such as university graduation, religious reasons, comedy, safety, or as a fashion accessory. Hats which incorporate mechanical features, such as visors, spikes, flaps, braces or beer holders shade into the broader category of headgear."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Chapeaux_en_peau_de_castor.jpg/330px-Chapeaux_en_peau_de_castor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hat"},{"title":"Chef","blocks":[{"text":"A chef is a professional cook and tradesperson who is proficient in many aspects of food preparation, often focusing on a particular cuisine. The word \"chef\" is derived from the term chef de cuisine, the director or head of a kitchen. Chefs can receive formal training from an institution, as well as by apprenticing with an experienced chef."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Ribot_Theodule_The_Cook_And_The_Cat-1.jpg/330px-Ribot_Theodule_The_Cook_And_The_Cat-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chef"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/The_Auxiliary_Territorial_Service_in_Britain_during_the_Second_World_War_TR2604.jpg/500px-The_Auxiliary_Territorial_Service_in_Britain_during_the_Second_World_War_TR2604.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/The_Auxiliary_Territorial_Service_in_Britain_during_the_Second_World_War_TR2604.jpg/1280px-The_Auxiliary_Territorial_Service_in_Britain_during_the_Second_World_War_TR2604.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/The_Auxiliary_Territorial_Service_in_Britain_during_the_Second_World_War_TR2604.jpg/500px-The_Auxiliary_Territorial_Service_in_Britain_during_the_Second_World_War_TR2604.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A chef and trainee during World War II","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Auxiliary_Territorial_Service_in_Britain_during_the_Second_World_War_TR2604.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://th